+<a name="fixed-pattern"></a>
+<h3>Fixed and Pattern Values</h3>
+<p>
+Profiles can constrain element values using <a href="elementdefinition-definitions.html#ElementDefinition.fixed_x_">fixed[x]</a>
+or <a href="elementdefinition-definitions.html#ElementDefinition.pattern_x_">pattern[x]</a>. A fixed value requires the
+instance value to match exactly; elements, attributes, ids, or extensions that are absent from the fixed value must also be
+absent from the instance. A pattern value is a partial example: values present in the pattern must be present and match in
+the instance, but additional values, such as extra codings, ids, or extensions, may also appear. A pattern declared on a
+repeating element applies to every repetition; use slicing if the pattern should apply only to one repetition or a subset of
+repetitions. See <a href="elementdefinition-examples.html#pattern-examples">Examples of Patterns</a> for valid and invalid
+examples.
+</p>
+
